  construction. A NO-GO fires the SAEOS-1 §7 falsifier and reverts the specification; it does
  **not** make this goal fail, and does not trigger the §4 rollback (see §4.3).

This restates the S-PROBE `deliverables`/`accept` block and the DESIGN §§0–9 without adding,
